>> title: Rice Pudding
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: rice, milk, pudding, stovetop, cinnamon
>> counters: Diner, Deli, Taquería
>> aka: arroz con leche
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: forgiving — once the egg is in it must not boil, because a pudding allowed to boil after that curdles and does not come back
>> step.1: simmer 15 min
>> step.2: simmer 30 min until creamy
>> step.5: cook 2 min, then stir in the raisins

Simmer @short-grain rice{1/2%cup}(100 g), @water{1%cup}(240 mL), @table salt{1/4%tsp} in a #heavy saucepan{} until the water is absorbed, ~{15%min}.

Stir @whole milk{4%cup}(960 mL), @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(65 g), @cinnamon stick{1%whole} into @&(~1)rice{} and simmer, stirring often, ~{30%min}.

Whisk @egg yolks{2%large}(37 g), @heavy cream{1/2%cup}(120 mL) smooth.

Temper @&(~1)yolks{} with @&(~2)hot rice pudding{}.

Cook @&(~1)pudding{} over low, stirring, for ~{2%min}, then stir in @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL), @raisins{1/3%cup}(50 g).
